{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task at all. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-axis comparison to config_001: same profile setting, same 'one-modality' simplicity, differing only in which modality is used. If image_only substantially outperforms rna_only, we know image features are informative and should prioritize multimodal/fusion experiments. If it performs similarly or worse, RNA is the primary signal and we should focus on RNA encoder and profile improvements before investing in fusion. This single result resolves the most consequential structural question in the search space and will most efficiently direct all subsequent experiments under a limited budget."
}

